  "why_c02_is_not_c06": [
    "C02 ordinary record selector kind is procurement-record-v1; its source ref prefix is sf-procurement:. C06 producer selector kind is procurement-confirmation-v1; its ref prefix is sf-procurement-c06:.",
    "Ordinary Procurement fields include ageDays and sourcing, which are outside the C06 supported field set. Copying C02 target.fields fails material scope validation.",
    "C06 requires scopeDefinitionVersion procurement-c06-v1, sorted unique supported fields, exact period and zero external materialDependencies.",
    "The C06 sourceRef.incarnation must identify a producer-registered material scope. The observer checks the original registry selector fields/period, its procurement-confirmation-v1 kind, physical incarnation, current authorized material projection and source fence.",
    "Removing unsupported fields or changing the prefix while preserving the ordinary C02 incarnation does not create the matching producer registry entry.",
    "C06 scopeFingerprint is derived by the producer from physical identity, selected values/states/currencies and material dependencies; it cannot be invented from the visible C02 amount or reused as a generic record digest.",
    "The user-confirmation command requires a private verified observation created by prepare under current authority and a storage CAS version; a locally constructed DTO is insufficient."
  ],
  "expected_future_journey": [
    "Use a real app producer selector to select one isolated Procurement request and supported material fields. Obtain issued scope/evidence under actual user authority.",
    "Prepare through mounted collaboration adapter; assert request identity, source incarnation, period, selected material values and producer fingerprint. Read storage version; confirm once through actual offered user control; assert exact confirmation/audit identity.",
    "Perform a real irrelevant domain edit, reread projection: valid unchanged-scope, original observedSourceVersion/audit unchanged, no extra canonical work.",
    "Perform a real material edit, reread projection: stale material-change or dependency-change with exact new evaluatedSourceVersion; exactly one canonical work item and stable identity across repeated reads.",
    "Revoke actual record access, then evaluate again: denial or unavailable per admission layer; no values, scope fingerprint, stale actionable links or new unauthorized work. Do not assert a single global HTTP code when the domain and host layers legitimately differ."
  ],
  "prohibited_substitutions": [
